    "commit": "aba4f5dade4700322370f84a8d727c8b0e0c7ed6",
    "commit_body": "Puts (<=25) with price above EMA50 are profit-taking pullbacks in\nuptrends, not breakdown setups. Fine-grained 5y sweep found WR30\ndeclines monotonically from 70.3% at ext=-10..-4 to 60.7% at ext>+10.\nLift proportional to how bearish the score is and how far above EMA50.\n\n5y diff-assess vs v20: <25 WR15 +2.7pp / WR30 +2.7pp; <15 WR15 +2.6pp /\nWR30 +2.3pp; <5 WR15 +5.4pp / WR30 +4.1pp. Ret30 flips positive at\nevery put tier. Cap30 up across all tiers (MAE tightens + MFE expands).\nMonotonic WR gradient restored across put buckets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "commit_short": "aba4f5da",
    "commit_subject": "Add ext-focal gradient dampener for puts above EMA50",
